\n- **Candidate\u202fD:** strong problem\u2011solving, concentration, and responsibility, yet also lacks any positive teamwork/communication evidence and exhibits a hot temper and loner attitude.\n- **Candidate\u202fA:** strong situational awareness and leadership, but is \u201cnot good at taking criticism,\u201d unorganized, and shows no explicit crew\u2011interaction strengths.\n**Main trade\u2011off:** C\u2019s communication difficulty and egocentric attitude versus the outright absence of teamwork strengths in B and D. The proven reliability, calmness, and positive crew atmosphere of C outweigh the communication concerns for the safety\u2011critical, long\u2011haul context.\n**Remaining uncertainty:** How frequently C\u2019s difficulty communicating ideas leads to operational misunderstandings or safety\u2011critical errors, and whether his unwillingness to further his education will limit adaptation to new procedures or technology.\n**What would change my vote:** Concrete evidence that C\u2019s communication issues cause regular crew friction or safety incidents, or new information revealing a candidate (especially B) possessing clear, positive teamwork or communication strengths that offset their other weaknesses.\nMETADATA_JSON:\n{\"agent\": \"agent_2\", \"vote\": \"Candidate C\"}", "thoughts": "We have obtained answer from Agent 3: no positive teamwork/communication strengths for B or D. Now we need to produce our public message as Agent 2, incorporating this new info, and our own provisional preference. Previously Agent 2 favored Candidate C. Now we have confirmation that B and D have no positive teamwork strengths. That strengthens C's position. We should mention that. Also note any uncertainties. Provide final vote."}
